+## Subtopics
+
+### Differentiable Primitive Assembly
+Uses differentiable set operations on primitive distances for occupancy. VDGS differs by using rasterization-based alpha compositing of Gaussians rather than set operations [13657-differentiable-primitive-assembly.md].
+
+### Point-NeRF Representation
+Uses point clouds with neural features. VDGS differs by using 3D Gaussians (with covariance) for shape and a NeRF-based MLP for view-dependent updates, whereas Point-NeRF typically uses points with local MLPs [15538-point-nerf-representation.md].
+
+### Frequency-Modulated Point Cloud Rendering
+Uses frequency modulation on point clouds. VDGS differs by using Gaussian splatting with hash-encoded NeRF updates for view-dependent appearance [15903-frequency-modulated-point-cloud-rendering.md].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Training and inference times are comparable to standard Gaussian Splatting, significantly faster than NeRF-based methods [S1]. On an NVIDIA RTX 3090, VDGS-30K training times are approximately 46 minutes for Mip-NeRF360, 30 minutes for Tanks & Temples, and 41 minutes for Deep Blending [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** The memory footprint is dominated by the Gaussian primitives and the hash grid [S1]. The hash grid uses $2^{14}$ entries with feature dimension 2, which is relatively small compared to dense voxel grids [S1].
-*   **Performance:**
-    *   **Mip-NeRF360:** SSIM 0.813, PSNR 27.64, LPIPS 0.220 [S1].
-    *   **Tanks and Temples:** SSIM 0.851, PSNR 24.02, LPIPS 0.176 [S1].
-    *   **Deep Blending:** SSIM 0.906, PSNR 29.54, LPIPS 0.243 [S1].
-    *   **Shiny Blender:** Avg PSNR 30.62 [S1].
-*   **Inference FPS:** On RTX 3090, VDGS-30K achieves 41.35 FPS (Mip-NeRF360), 38.53 FPS (Tanks & Temples), and 44.72 FPS (Deep Blending) [S1].
-*   **Strengths:** Fast training and inference; ability to model view-dependent effects (reflections, transparency) without increasing training time significantly compared to GS [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires tuning of hash grid parameters; joint optimization of color and opacity may be unstable [S1].
